{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789553562,"nonce":"4jonUQ13cy1uIr+ZlTgnDsG2kAE=","title":"LLVM promotion crashes after short Python loops","message":"Build zypy with --features llvm-backend, then run ZYPY_LLVM=1 target/release/zypy run crates/zyntax_python/conformance/class/instance_arguments.py. It prints the expected output and exits 139 (SIGSEGV); inference/list_fields.py behaves the same. With ZYNTAX_OSR_TRACE=1, a short loop requests tier 2 and the process dies after \"[osr] llvm install tier=2 functions=3\", during MCJIT installation or shutdown. These loops have only a handful of iterations, so eager OSR compilation is wasted even when it succeeds.\n\nThe normal zypy CLI leaves LLVM off until explicitly selected. The speed harness selects and verifies LLVM. Investigate the MCJIT promotion lifetime and defer OSR work for loops that do not become hot. Re-enable LLVM for the full conformance suite once both cases exit cleanly.","files":null}]}